[
  {
    "id": "S06",
    "act": 2,
    "title": "2 · Fingerprint it",
    "transitionIn": "wipe",
    "shots": [
      {
        "visual": "ActTitle",
        "props": {
          "act": "Part two",
          "title": "Fingerprint it",
          "tone": "amber"
        },
        "sfx": [
          "whoosh"
        ],
        "beats": [
          {
            "id": "S06_01",
            "vo": "Checking without reading back is what a cryptographic hash does."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "visual": "HashGrinder",
        "props": {
          "input": "mango@123",
          "algo": "SHA-256",
          "hex": "81c68634d1b211e0d5632839f7efc8601c743f1ef0c94da8220e26ab221efff1",
          "note": "64 characters, every time",
          "caption": "No way back. Only guess, hash, compare."
        },
        "beats": [
          {
            "id": "S06_02",
            "vo": "It turns any text into a fingerprint of fixed length."
          },
          {
            "id": "S06_03",
            "vo": "Feed it mango at the rate one two three, and SHA two fifty-six gives back sixty-four characters, a jumble of digits and letters. It looks like noise."
          },
          {
            "id": "S06_04",
            "vo": "And there's no practical way to run it backwards. An attacker can still guess, hash the guess, and compare."
          }
        ],
        "sfx": [
          "tick"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "S07",
    "act": 2,
    "title": "The avalanche",
    "transitionIn": "cut",
    "shots": [
      {
        "visual": "Avalanche",
        "props": {
          "a": "hunter2",
          "b": "hunter3",
          "diffAt": 6,
          "hexA": "f52fbd32b2b3b86ff88ef6c490628285f482af15ddcb29541f94bcf526a3f6c7",
          "hexB": "fb8c2e2b85ca81eb4350199faddd983cb26af3064614e737ea9f479621cfa57a",
          "caption": "One character apart. Nothing alike."
        },
        "beats": [
          {
            "id": "S07_01",
            "vo": "Change one character, and the fingerprint changes all over."
          },
          {
            "id": "S07_02",
            "vo": "Hunter two and hunter three differ by a single digit. The differences are scattered across the whole fingerprint."
          },
          {
            "id": "S07_03",
            "vo": "In this pair, one hundred and forty-six of the two hundred and fifty-six bits flipped."
          },
          {
            "id": "S07_04",
            "vo": "So a near miss doesn't look like a near miss."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "S08",
    "act": 2,
    "title": "Login, with hashes",
    "transitionIn": "push",
    "shots": [
      {
        "visual": "LoginMatch",
        "props": {
          "input": "mango@123",
          "email": "you@mail.com",
          "hex": "81c68634d1b211e0d5632839f7efc8601c743f1ef0c94da8220e26ab221efff1",
          "caption": "A leak gives fingerprints, not passwords"
        },
        "beats": [
          {
            "id": "S08_01",
            "vo": "So the app stores the fingerprint instead of the password."
          },
          {
            "id": "S08_02",
            "vo": "When you log in, it hashes what you just typed, and compares the two fingerprints."
          },
          {
            "id": "S08_03",
            "vo": "They match, so the app lets you in."
          },
          {
            "id": "S08_04",
            "vo": "If that table leaks, the attacker gets fingerprints, not passwords. That sounds airtight. LinkedIn found out it wasn't."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "S09",
    "act": 2,
    "title": "LinkedIn, 2012",
    "transitionIn": "fade",
    "shots": [
      {
        "visual": "TextStack",
        "props": {
          "kicker": "LinkedIn · 2012",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "6,458,020 password hashes posted online",
              "step": 0,
              "size": 64
            },
            {
              "text": "SHA-1 · no salt",
              "mono": true,
              "tone": "red",
              "step": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "beats": [
          {
            "id": "S09_01",
            "vo": "In twenty twelve, a file of about six and a half million LinkedIn password hashes was posted online."
          },
          {
            "id": "S09_02",
            "vo": "They were SHA one hashes, with nothing added. Unsalted."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "visual": "LookupWall",
        "props": {
          "stolen": "f14d5ba7f5892b8cb2549dea72287ee3692bb297",
          "rows": [
            {
              "password": "123456",
              "hash": "7c4a8d09ca3762af61e59520943dc26494f8941b"
            },
            {
              "password": "password",
              "hash": "5baa61e4c9b93f3f0682250b6cf8331b7ee68fd8"
            },
            {
              "password": "12345678",
              "hash": "7c222fb2927d828af22f592134e8932480637c0d"
            },
            {
              "password": "qwerty",
              "hash": "b1b3773a05c0ed0176787a4f1574ff0075f7521e"
            },
            {
              "password": "iloveyou",
              "hash": "ee8d8728f435fd550f83852aabab5234ce1da528"
            },
            {
              "password": "111111",
              "hash": "3d4f2bf07dc1be38b20cd6e46949a1071f9d0e3d"
            },
            {
              "password": "mango@123",
              "hash": "f14d5ba7f5892b8cb2549dea72287ee3692bb297"
            }
          ],
          "caption": "Your password is the row next to it"
        },
        "beats": [
          {
            "id": "S09_03",
            "vo": "That matters because the same password always produces the same fingerprint."
          },
          {
            "id": "S09_04",
            "vo": "Attackers don't need to reverse anything. They hash millions of common passwords once, ahead of time, and keep the results in a lookup table."
          },
          {
            "id": "S09_05",
            "vo": "Then they just search. If your fingerprint is in their table, your password is the row next to it."
          }
        ],
        "sfx": [
          "tick"
        ],
        "sfxBeat": [
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "visual": "StatGrid",
        "props": {
          "title": "LinkedIn breach",
          "items": [
            {
              "value": "6.5M",
              "label": "hashes posted · 2012",
              "tone": "amber",
              "step": 0
            },
            {
              "value": "117M",
              "label": "emails and passwords · LinkedIn, 2016",
              "tone": "red",
              "step": 0
            }
          ]
        },
        "beats": [
          {
            "id": "S09_06",
            "vo": "Four years later, LinkedIn said it believed the breach was far bigger: a hundred and seventeen million emails and passwords."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "S10",
    "act": 2,
    "title": "Salt",
    "transitionIn": "zoom",
    "shots": [
      {
        "visual": "TextStack",
        "props": {
          "kicker": "the fix",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "Salt",
              "size": 150,
              "tone": "teal",
              "step": 0
            },
            {
              "text": "a random string, unique to each user",
              "serif": false,
              "size": 44,
              "step": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "stored next to the hash · not secret",
              "serif": false,
              "size": 40,
              "tone": "slate",
              "step": 2
            }
          ]
        },
        "beats": [
          {
            "id": "S10_01",
            "vo": "The fix is called salting."
          },
          {
            "id": "S10_02",
            "vo": "Each password gets its own random string, mixed in before hashing. That string is the salt."
          },
          {
            "id": "S10_03",
            "vo": "It isn't secret. It's stored right next to the hash. Its job is to make the same password hash differently for every user."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "visual": "SaltGrinder",
        "props": {
          "password": "mango@123",
          "users": [
            {
              "name": "Asha",
              "salt": "9f2c4a71",
              "hash": "fb9d05563ec1fbbdebc0c48ed14a7db7087102a8373e44fc54ad57d8b1ed0401"
            },
            {
              "name": "You",
              "salt": "e05b13d8",
              "hash": "324ce3f954f77c01e68347a9e85134bc81b2455b7a852fa022ea6c4b0efea9a8"
            }
          ],
          "caption": "A table built in advance would need one per salt"
        },
        "beats": [
          {
            "id": "S10_04",
            "vo": "Two people who both chose mango at the rate one two three now get completely different fingerprints."
          },
          {
            "id": "S10_05",
            "vo": "As long as salts are long and random, a table built in advance stops working. It would need a separate table for every salt."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
]